1
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:22,520
As discussed in our last meeting,
for the Foresta Collection concept,

2
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:25,320
which focuses on the linework of
flowers and leaves,

3
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,960
I'd like to present the designs
for your consideration.

4
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:33,920
These are the ninth set of initial sketches.

5
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,160
This piece is a necklace,

6
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:37,880
featuring a square-link chain.

7
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:40,440
There are also earrings and a ring.

8
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,960
The overall collection will look
something like this.

9
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:59,080
If you'd like to make changes
or any adjustments,

10
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,320
please let me know.

11
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:15,600
I'd like to do a few more styles.

12
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,120
Women have different tastes and styles.

13
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,680
Some are sweet,

14
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:28,120
some are cool,

15
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:29,360
some are refined.

16
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,320
Everyone has their own preferences.

17
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:42,760
What is it, Cream?

18
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,440
Then please come up with
some additional designs,

19
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:47,800
and let's schedule
a wrap-up meeting for next week.

20
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,520
Certainly, Chairwoman.

21
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:57,880
What is it?

22
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,520
Mr. Sam has caused trouble again.

23
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,120
Again?

24
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,720
Yes, again.

25
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,240
When will she ever learn?

26
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:11,640
Is this nurse quitting too?

27
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:13,240
Yes.

28
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,560
Ms. Nueng tried to talk her into staying,

29
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:16,920
but it didn't work.

30
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,880
Same as always.

31
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,480
Sometimes I wonder

32
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,400
why I have to clean up their mess.

33
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,800
Find a new nurse as soon as possible.

34
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:33,600
Yes,

35
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,120
but it may take some time.

36
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:39,960
It took us a while to find the last one.

37
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,040
I don't care.

38
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,640
Make it happen faster.

39
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,760
My mother needs someone looking after her 24/7.

40
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,800
I don't care what it costs.

41
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:50,400
Yes.

42
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,880
Just find a temporary nurse in the meantime.

43
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:55,480
Ask Nueng and Cream to help out too.

44
00:03:56,079 --> 00:03:57,120
That's all.

45
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,440
Yes, Ms. Song.

46
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,640
Look, it's Dr. Smith!

47
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,440
So handsome, with that face card!

48
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:27,440
What's card?

49
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,920
It means he's super handsome.

50
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:31,920
Hello, Doctor.

51
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,080
Hello.

52
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,760
What's up, little brother?

53
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:42,840
Hi.

54
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:44,880
You see…

55
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,800
Ms. Song's private nurse has quit. Again.

56
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,040
How many is that now?

57
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,520
Seven.

58
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:55,080
So Mr. Sam is every nurse's worst nightmare.

59
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:59,040
Are you just calling to get me to buy you lunch?

60
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,320
It's not that.

61
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,680
I need your help.

62
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,680
Can you help me find a nurse?

63
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,320
Nah.

64
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:10,960
If I send someone over
and Mr. Sam gives them trouble again,

65
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,280
it'll ruin my reputation.

66
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,840
That's why I've never asked you before.

67
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,040
But this time I'm at a dead end.

68
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:20,320
I don't want Ms. Song
getting stressed out over this again.

69
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,000
You're really worried about her.

70
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,880
Have you even made any progress with her?

71
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,880
Smith, I'm serious.

72
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,040
Yeah, I know.

73
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,560
I'll see what I can do.

74
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,440
But no promises, okay?

75
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:35,960
That's already a big help.

76
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,960
There you go.

77
00:05:54,159 --> 00:05:56,320
Once you're done here,

78
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,600
head up to Finance on the fourth floor.

79
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,280
We'll see you
at your next appointment, okay?

80
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:05,960
Excuse me.

81
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:16,600
I appreciate the thought,
but you really don't need to do that.

82
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:17,680
Thank you.

83
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:24,200
I need to do something about this.

84
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,040
What was that?

85
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,240
Oh, nothing.

86
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,640
I think I know someone.

87
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:33,920
What about the salary?

88
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,360
Name your price.

89
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,880
Ms. Song will meet their demands.

90
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,360
Okay.

91
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:42,320
I'll call you if I find someone.

92
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,480
Thank you.

93
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,680
That's all for now.

94
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,680
Professor, could you sign
this medical certificate?

95
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:57,000
Sure.

96
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:03,360
-Here you go.
-This one too, Professor.

97
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,240
Of course.

98
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,560
-There you go.
-Thank you.

99
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,720
Ms. Uttawadee.

100
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:16,320
Yes, Professor?

101
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,640
Could you come to my office later?

102
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:19,840
Right now?

103
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,520
Not yet.

104
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,520
I have to make rounds in Room 1608 first.

105
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,920
Okay.

106
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,600
Thanks.

107
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,920
Oops, my hand slipped.

108
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,400
Oops, my hand slipped.

109
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:12,640
-Hey! I haven't even touched that yet!
-Yeah.

110
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,120
Maybe it's contagious.

111
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,160
How's your mother doing, Oh?

112
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:50,960
Well,

113
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,480
ever since they found the new cancer cells,

114
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:56,800
she's been taking it pretty hard, as you know.

115
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,320
Don't lose heart.

116
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:05,000
She beat it last time.

117
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,560
She'll get through this too.

118
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,240
I hope so.

119
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,600
Let me know if you need anything.

120
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:14,720
Maybe I can help.

121
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,040
Thank you.

122
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:23,320
You'll need lots of money
for her treatment, right?

123
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:26,760
Yes.

124
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:30,720
My sister and I are trying to earn more

125
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:33,080
to cover the medical expenses.

126
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,080
Hmm.

127
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:41,760
If you had a chance
to earn several times more than you do now,

128
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:44,360
would you be willing to leave this job for it?

129
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:46,840
What kind of job?

130
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:50,600
Private nursing for an elderly woman at home.

131
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,440
She's someone I really respect.

132
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,720
You'd have one day off a week.

133
00:09:57,320 --> 00:10:00,120
The pay is almost five times
what you're making now.

134
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,280
May I ask about her condition?

135
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,760
She has paraplegia

136
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:09,160
and stage-two Alzheimer's.

137
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,800
She needs around-the-clock support.

138
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,360
Is her condition serious?

139
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,080
Not that bad.

140
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:20,640
Her daughter just wants someone there
to keep her safe.

141
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,560
I see.

142
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,520
When would I start?

143
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:28,760
Honestly, they need someone to start right away.

144
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:32,120
It's a good opportunity,
so I thought I'd let you know.

145
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,480
Okay.

146
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,160
As for your mother,

147
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:47,000
I'll check on her regularly.

148
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,440
Don't worry.

149
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,400
Thank you.

150
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:54,840
I'll give you my answer as soon as I can.

151
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,240
Sure.

152
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,920
Then I'll get going.

153
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,640
Of course.

154
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,640
Let's see if those guys still try to hit on her.

155
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,560
Did you find someone?

156
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:18,360
Yes.

157
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:21,120
She'll discuss it with her family first,

158
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,720
but I don't think there'll be a problem.

159
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,120
As for the salary,

160
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:28,480
offer her 10% more than the last nurse.

161
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:29,840
No problem.

162
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,320
I'll tell Ms. Song right away.

163
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,800
So eager to win her favor…
or maybe her heart?

164
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,760
Smith.

165
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,800
Yeah, yeah. I know.

166
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:43,960
Come on, everyone! This is the last piece!

167
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:46,600
I'm ending the livestream in five minutes.

168
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,480
You won't find this price anywhere else!

169
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:50,320
It's a special deal.

170
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:53,120
Everyone needs this color. Don't miss it.

171
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,920
It's so pretty!

172
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,440
It looks even better in person!

173
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,320
Add it to your basket now!

174
00:11:58,640 --> 00:12:02,840
You'll also get a coupon for 50% off!

175
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:03,840
See?

176
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:07,000
You're getting such a great deal
with my livestream.

177
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:09,160
And up next, we have something

178
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,920
you've all been waiting for.

179
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,320
The camisole set!

180
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,920
This camisole set

181
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,320
comes in a classy purple pattern.

182
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:21,720
It'll give you a sweet and chic vibe.

183
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,640
It looks amazing on camera!

184
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,880
I've got it in various colors and sizes.

185
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:28,520
You can order this set
even outside the livestream!

186
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,800
That's it for today, everyone!

187
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:33,840
See you next time! Bye!

188
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,760
Finally.

189
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,720
Here. Have some water first.

190
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,000
-Thanks.
-Tired?

191
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,960
No, but I didn't sell much today.

192
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,880
I wonder where everyone went.

193
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:55,960
At least I'll still get my livestream hours.

194
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:58,080
-Right.
-Hmm?

195
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,240
Let me show you something.

196
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:08,240
Hold on.

197
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,480
Wow, that's a lot!

198
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:16,720
Right?

199
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:20,160
I'll use this money for Mom's next treatment

200
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,960
and groceries.

201
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:24,640
Hmm.

202
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,880
Nothing for yourself?

203
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,520
Mm.

204
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,440
Nope. I don't need anything.

205
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,520
I have plenty of sponsored clothes.

206
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:36,120
You want some?

207
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,040
You keep them.

208
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,520
I don't go anywhere anyway.

209
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:42,520
Just work and home.

210
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,560
True.

211
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,200
I still have to pack everything up.

212
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:51,440
Your shoulders sore?

213
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,600
A little.

214
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:54,400
Really?

215
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,120
Thanks!

216
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:02,240
By the way, do you have any tutoring today?

217
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,960
Not anymore.

218
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,920
Hmm…

219
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:09,640
-Ong?
-Yeah?

220
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:11,440
Can we talk?

221
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:16,480
Professor Smith just offered me a job.

222
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:19,320
A job? What kind?

223
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,640
Private nursing.

224
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:24,680
I'd have to live at the patient's home.

225
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:25,800
Wait.

226
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:27,480
Is the patient a man or a woman?

227
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:28,920
A woman.

228
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:34,200
I'd get Sundays off.

229
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,960
Whoa, that's a demanding job.

230
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:39,520
How much does it pay?

231
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,240
With that kind of money, take it!

232
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:54,080
I'll even help you pack.

233
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,760
Take everything you need!

234
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:56,960
No hesitation at all, huh?

235
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,720
Go! Shoo, shoo!

236
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,320
I'll pack everything for you right now.

237
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,520
How's that?

238
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,200
Hmm…

239
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:05,800
What about Mom?

240
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:08,200
Can you take care of her?

241
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:09,840
And what about your studies?

242
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,080
Don't worry.

243
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:14,840
I only have my thesis left,
and then I'll graduate.

244
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:17,120
Just go. I'll take care of Mom.

245
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,120
If we're earning this much every month,

246
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,720
you won't have to tire yourself
with tutoring anymore.

247
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:25,720
But what about your job at the hospital?

248
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:27,960
I'm only working part-time.

249
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,560
It shouldn't be a problem.

250
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:31,640
Professor Smith

251
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:34,360
already promised to help check on Mom too.

252
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:38,760
Oh, but doesn't he

253
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,720
already come here regularly?

254
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,800
I just wanted you to know.

255
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,160
Hmm.

256
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:51,320
When will you give him your answer?

257
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,880
I wanted to discuss it with you first.

258
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,360
Then I'll talk to Mom.

259
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:57,600
I can give him my answer tomorrow.

260
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:01,240
Okay. Let's go see Mom, then.

261
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:07,600
Just take the job if you want to.

262
00:16:07,680 --> 00:16:09,920
I'll be just fine with Ong.

263
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:11,880
You won't get lonely, will you?

264
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,480
I'll miss you, of course.

265
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:15,880
But I don't want you

266
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:18,040
to turn down a good opportunity
because of me.

267
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,760
If your dad were still here,

268
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:23,000
he'd be so proud of you.

269
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:25,720
What about me?

270
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,400
What about me, huh?

271
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,360
I'm proud of you too.

272
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:38,040
I have such wonderful daughters.

273
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:43,960
Now go take a shower

274
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,320
and get some rest.

275
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,360
-Yes.
-Okay.

276
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,880
I'm going to get some rest too.

277
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,480
Let me take that for you.

278
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:19,920
Ong, you can shower first.

279
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,319
Let me know when you're done.

280
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,440
Okay.

281
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:51,560
Someday,

282
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:54,040
things will get better for us.

283
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:06,400
I'll take the job.

284
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:08,400
Wonderful!

285
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:11,120
They've sent over a contract.

286
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:12,640
Take a look.

287
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,000
But first,

288
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:27,040
there are a few things I need to tell you.

289
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:29,640
What things?

290
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,440
The son of the family

291
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,480
is quite a womanizer.

292
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:39,360
He tends to give the nurses a hard time,

293
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:42,520
which is why so many of them quit.

294
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,240
But don't worry.

295
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,520
You'll be perfectly safe.

296
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:53,160
I've told everyone there

297
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,520
that you're my girlfriend,

298
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:59,160
so they'll make sure
you're well looked after.

299
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:01,080
You told them we're dating?

300
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:02,800
Is it really okay?

301
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,800
What about your reputation?

302
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,280
Not at all.

303
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:09,760
I'm happy to help.

304
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,920
I'd love for this to become real too.

305
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:19,040
What was that?

306
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:23,800
I said it's for the best.

307
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:27,160
Anyway, apart from the playboy son,

308
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:29,560
everyone there is perfectly nice.

309
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:34,360
You can focus on your work
and save money for your mother's treatment.

310
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:41,520
Okay.

311
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:43,280
If you say so,

312
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:44,640
I'll take it.

313
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:47,880
All right. Read through the contract first.

314
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,600
Everything will be as discussed.

315
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:53,240
But the employer's details aren't included.

316
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:56,360
If you'd prefer,

317
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,840
you can sign it tomorrow when you arrive.

318
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,280
That's fine.

319
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:03,560
Today or tomorrow makes no difference.

320
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,840
I trust you, Professor.

321
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,360
Thank you.

322
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,480
One more thing.

323
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,640
To keep up our fake relationship,

324
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:20,240
you'll have to start calling me Smith

325
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,280
instead of Professor.

326
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
I see.

327
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:28,320
Okay…

328
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:30,080
Smith.

329
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:33,400
Good.

330
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,680
I thought you were joking!

331
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:45,000
So you're really taking it?

332
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:47,000
Yeah.

333
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:49,400
Why, Oh? Why?

334
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,200
It's so sudden!

335
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:53,400
What am I supposed to do without you?

336
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:56,320
Who am I going to have lunch with?

337
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:02,200
It's not like we see each other every day.

338
00:21:02,680 --> 00:21:04,320
We hardly ever work the same shifts.

339
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,680
But we still get to see each other, okay?

340
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:11,000
I'm sad, you know.

341
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,120
Okay, okay.

342
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,880
I'll come by on my days off.

343
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,480
We can grab a meal together.

344
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:18,640
Listen,

345
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,880
you have to stay in touch.

346
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:23,800
Don't disappear on me, okay?

347
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:27,000
Sure. I'll call and keep you updated.

348
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:28,120
Good?

349
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,200
Fine.

350
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:44,920
What?!

351
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:48,320
They require 120 days' notice
before resigning?

352
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:51,640
That's outrageous!

353
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,640
It's usually only 30 days.

354
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:57,240
And the penalty is five times your salary?

355
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:00,480
That's brutal.

356
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:02,800
I'll be fine.

357
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:05,400
I usually stay at my jobs for a long time anyway.

358
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:10,440
Yeah, Superwoman.

359
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:12,680
You're good at everything.

360
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:36,680
SIGNATURE
MISS UTTAWADEE SENTANUN

361
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:40,880
Here are the documents.

362
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:52,680
The new nurse will arrive
at Mrs. Pinthong's house

363
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,080
around 1 p.m. tomorrow.

364
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:56,440
Smith will take her there.

365
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:00,480
Is she close to Smith?

366
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:03,080
He recommended her
and is even taking her there himself.

367
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:04,760
Well…

368
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:06,640
You see…

369
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:08,720
She's his girlfriend.

370
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:12,360
Have I not mentioned that?

371
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:15,160
I'm sorry.

372
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,760
I thought I'd told you everything.

373
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,720
Maybe I just forgot.

374
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:27,200
Having Smith's girlfriend work there
should be fine too.

375
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:29,000
It solves the problem with Sam.

376
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,280
He wouldn't dare mess with his girlfriend.

377
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:35,040
Right.

378
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:37,560
Do I have any appointments around that time?

379
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:41,240
Just an internal meeting with the design
and marketing teams.

380
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:42,880
Reschedule it.

381
00:23:42,960 --> 00:23:44,280
I want to meet Smith

382
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:46,160
and thank him for his help.

383
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:48,600
I'll take the new nurse
to meet my mother, too.

384
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:50,520
Of course.

385
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:40,280
Please let this one stay for a long time.

386
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:16,680
Where are you?

387
00:25:16,760 --> 00:25:18,200
I'm waiting in the living room.

388
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,280
I just parked.

389
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:21,760
Give me a moment.

390
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:23,360
Ms. Song will be here soon.

391
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:24,760
Okay. See you.

392
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:26,240
Right.

393
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:32,920
Just wait here for a bit, Oh.

394
00:25:55,440 --> 00:25:56,600
Damn it.

395
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:19,800
Has the new nurse arrived?

396
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:21,240
Um… Ms. Song,

397
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:22,760
I think

398
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:24,920
you should visit Mrs. Pinthong first.

399
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:25,920
Why?

400
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:27,560
Hasn't the nurse arrived yet?

401
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:28,800
She has.

402
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:32,920
Then let's meet her
before taking her to see my mother.

403
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:35,800
But…

404
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:38,120
You haven't visited Mrs. Pinthong in a few days.

405
00:26:38,520 --> 00:26:39,960
Maybe we should see her first.

406
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:42,080
No. Let's take care of one thing at a time.

407
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,280
Uh…

408
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:47,520
Move aside.

409
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:48,920
All right.

410
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,960
Hello, Ms. Song.

411
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:06,200
Here's the contract.

412
00:27:33,880 --> 00:27:35,520
Section 15,

413
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:40,040
paragraph one of the Civil
and Commercial Code states that,

414
00:27:40,120 --> 00:27:41,040
"Personality begins

415
00:27:41,120 --> 00:27:43,520
with the full completion of birth
as a living child,

416
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:45,000
and ends with death."

417
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:48,680
That means two conditions must be met.

418
00:27:48,760 --> 00:27:51,480
This will definitely be on the exam.
The professor emphasized it.

419
00:27:51,560 --> 00:27:52,480
Did you memorize it?

420
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,640
I think I've got it.

421
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:55,320
I'll come back to this.

422
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:56,280
Okay.

423
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:57,360
Okay.

424
00:27:57,440 --> 00:28:00,320
Let's move on. I think we're done with this part.

425
00:28:37,520 --> 00:28:38,520
Hmm?

426
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:43,080
What's wrong?

427
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:45,040
Do you have any questions?

428
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:46,200
No.

429
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:48,200
Open it.

430
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:51,400
-Open?
-Mm-hmm.

431
00:28:56,160 --> 00:28:58,120
WILL YOU GO OUT WITH ME?

432
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:33,280
Open it.

433
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:52,280
WILL YOU GO OUT WITH ME?
OK!

434
00:29:52,680 --> 00:29:54,120
Okay? Yes!

435
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:01,240
Hey!

436
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:05,720
Stop!

437
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:07,960
We're dating now, okay?

438
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:09,280
Yeah.

439
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:15,040
Stop already!

440
00:30:16,120 --> 00:30:17,640
Let's get back to studying.

441
00:30:18,040 --> 00:30:19,320
I don't want to study anymore.

442
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:21,320
We have to, or you'll fail.

443
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:24,640
Fine. Let's do it.

444
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:28,520
Keep reading. I'll be quiet, okay?

445
00:31:46,680 --> 00:31:47,960
Oops.

446
00:31:51,320 --> 00:31:52,360
Hmm…

447
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:57,960
Give it back!

448
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:00,960
-No.
-Give it here.

449
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:02,960
Nope.

450
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,880
Don't you want to see me become a nurse?

451
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:14,840
Hmm?

452
00:32:17,360 --> 00:32:19,040
Please?

453
00:32:19,120 --> 00:32:21,200
Pretty please?

454
00:32:22,120 --> 00:32:23,120
Please?

455
00:32:24,280 --> 00:32:25,440
-Please?
-Fine.

456
00:32:26,600 --> 00:32:27,600
Thanks.

457
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:09,600
Oh…

458
00:33:10,720 --> 00:33:12,560
If there's anything I can do,

459
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:14,200
you have to tell me.

460
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:19,480
Thanks.

461
00:33:21,840 --> 00:33:23,000
I think I can manage.

462
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:27,880
Really, Song.

463
00:33:29,360 --> 00:33:31,000
I still have my mom and my sister.

464
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:33,640
I'll be okay.

465
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:35,920
And you have me.

466
00:33:39,400 --> 00:33:40,800
If you need any help,

467
00:33:41,320 --> 00:33:42,640
you have to tell me.

468
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:47,440
Oh…

469
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:51,560
promise me.

470
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:54,120
If anything happens,

471
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,520
you have to tell me.

472
00:33:58,240 --> 00:33:59,360
I will.

473
00:33:59,960 --> 00:34:01,400
I promise.

474
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:02,680
You promised, okay?

475
00:34:04,200 --> 00:34:05,240
If you don't tell me,

476
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:07,520
I'll be so mad.

477
00:34:09,639 --> 00:34:10,520
Mm-hmm.

478
00:34:12,120 --> 00:34:13,639
No matter what it is,

479
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:14,840
big or small,

480
00:34:18,440 --> 00:34:20,120
we'll get through it together.

481
00:34:38,199 --> 00:34:39,199
Oh!

482
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:42,080
Oh!

483
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:44,120
Oh!

484
00:34:44,199 --> 00:34:45,239
Oh!

485
00:34:48,040 --> 00:34:49,040
Oh…

486
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:51,199
Why did you pull away?

487
00:34:53,520 --> 00:34:54,960
What's wrong?

488
00:34:55,040 --> 00:34:56,880
You've been avoiding me all day.

489
00:34:58,960 --> 00:34:59,960
I'm tired of it.

490
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:01,520
Tired?

491
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:04,960
Of what?

492
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:07,920
Of you, obviously.

493
00:35:12,680 --> 00:35:13,800
You're joking, right?

494
00:35:14,720 --> 00:35:16,600
You're just teasing me.

495
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:18,640
Is this a prank?

496
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:20,440
Was it funny?

497
00:35:27,560 --> 00:35:28,560
Look…

498
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:32,880
If I've done something wrong,

499
00:35:34,080 --> 00:35:35,400
just tell me, okay?

500
00:35:36,320 --> 00:35:37,760
I told you. I'm tired of you.

501
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:39,640
I'm tired of living like this.

502
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:41,880
I want a rich girlfriend I can show off.

503
00:35:41,960 --> 00:35:43,680
I want to eat at fancy places,

504
00:35:43,760 --> 00:35:45,160
ride around in a sports car,

505
00:35:45,240 --> 00:35:46,840
and carry designer bags.

506
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:49,160
You never give me any of that.

507
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:05,960
Is this who you really are?

508
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:08,440
Yes.

509
00:36:08,520 --> 00:36:09,680
This is who I am.

510
00:36:10,720 --> 00:36:12,760
I've been playing nice for so long,

511
00:36:12,840 --> 00:36:15,160
hoping you'd spend money on me.

512
00:36:15,240 --> 00:36:16,560
But in the end,

513
00:36:19,120 --> 00:36:20,440
you just can't afford it.

514
00:36:26,040 --> 00:36:28,520
So you want to eat at fancy restaurants?

515
00:36:28,600 --> 00:36:30,240
Ride around in a sports car?

516
00:36:30,320 --> 00:36:31,640
Carry designer bags?

517
00:36:32,640 --> 00:36:33,760
Yeah.

518
00:36:34,480 --> 00:36:35,760
Do you want necklaces,

519
00:36:35,840 --> 00:36:37,480
rings, and watches too?

520
00:36:37,560 --> 00:36:38,480
I do!

521
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:40,480
Can you afford any of that?

522
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:42,360
Probably not.

523
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:44,320
Even for my birthday,

524
00:36:44,400 --> 00:36:47,120
all you could give me
was a pathetic handmade card.

525
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:49,240
Do you know how embarrassed I felt
in front of my friends?

526
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:51,320
Have you ever even asked what I want?

527
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:53,280
You're embarrassed?

528
00:36:56,440 --> 00:36:59,040
I spent the whole day making that card.

529
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:02,360
That piece of paper

530
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:05,080
might as well be trash.

531
00:37:07,160 --> 00:37:08,240
Trash?

532
00:37:12,240 --> 00:37:14,800
So you're just like everyone else,

533
00:37:15,160 --> 00:37:16,280
chasing money.

534
00:37:16,680 --> 00:37:17,720
Yes.

535
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:19,640
This is who I am.

536
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:21,240
Always have been.

537
00:37:22,960 --> 00:37:25,240
We shouldn't waste each other's time.

538
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:29,960
Let's break up.

539
00:37:30,600 --> 00:37:31,640
Oh!

540
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:40,320
Don't go. Please.

541
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,280
Let go of me.

542
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:43,720
Don't go.

543
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,040
-Let go!
-Oh!

544
00:37:45,120 --> 00:37:46,640
You're so annoying!

545
00:37:51,240 --> 00:37:52,440
From now on,

546
00:37:53,840 --> 00:37:55,960
don't ever come into my life again!

547
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:01,880
♪ I notice every glance ♪

548
00:38:01,960 --> 00:38:02,920
Oh!

549
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:06,920
♪ The way you look at me ♪

550
00:38:07,440 --> 00:38:12,360
♪ And what they're hiding inside ♪

551
00:38:12,640 --> 00:38:16,160
♪ I think we might be the same ♪

552
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:20,320
♪ Hiding our true feelings ♪

553
00:38:20,400 --> 00:38:23,240
♪ Not wanting them to come out ♪

554
00:38:23,600 --> 00:38:26,800
♪ But the closer we get ♪

555
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:30,760
♪ The more my heart wavers ♪

556
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:35,280
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

557
00:38:35,360 --> 00:38:37,640
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

558
00:38:37,720 --> 00:38:41,400
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

559
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:46,560
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

560
00:38:46,640 --> 00:38:49,840
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

561
00:38:49,920 --> 00:38:54,360
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

562
00:38:54,440 --> 00:38:56,040
Why?

563
00:38:56,120 --> 00:38:58,760
-♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪
-Why?

564
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:02,360
I'm sorry.

565
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:08,840
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪

566
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:31,360
Sarttra.

567
00:39:40,080 --> 00:39:42,360
Something must have come up with Ms. Song.

568
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:44,280
Please have a seat, Oh.

569
00:39:58,400 --> 00:39:59,960
You know that woman?

570
00:40:00,360 --> 00:40:01,240
Uh…

571
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:02,360
I think…

572
00:40:02,440 --> 00:40:03,600
I think I do.

573
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:06,480
Then why did you bring her into this house?

574
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:10,600
Ms. Song, I'm truly sorry.
I didn't check beforehand.

575
00:40:10,680 --> 00:40:12,400
Smith recommended her,

576
00:40:12,480 --> 00:40:14,200
saying she was his girlfriend,

577
00:40:16,680 --> 00:40:18,200
so I didn't look into it properly.

578
00:40:18,840 --> 00:40:21,000
Should I go cancel the contract?

579
00:40:23,840 --> 00:40:24,920
Give it to me.

580
00:40:36,400 --> 00:40:40,680
TERMINATION OF THE CONTRACT AND PENALTIES
A PENALTY EQUIVALENT TO FIVE TIMES THE SALARY

581
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:45,880
Contract termination…

582
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:55,880
SIGNATURE
MISS UTTAWADEE SENTANUN

583
00:41:21,520 --> 00:41:22,680
It's been a long time.

584
00:41:23,440 --> 00:41:25,280
So this is what you've been after.

585
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:33,200
I'd like to turn down this job.

586
00:41:34,040 --> 00:41:36,320
This contract isn't complete anyway.

587
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:38,040
Wait, Oh.

588
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:39,200
What's going on?

589
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,240
Not complete?

590
00:41:47,200 --> 00:41:48,640
Which part isn't?

591
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:07,040
SIGNATURE
EMPLOYER

592
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:13,360
There.

593
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:14,760
Now it's complete.

594
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:17,320
-But--
-Right.

595
00:42:17,800 --> 00:42:20,720
I heard you say you wanted to turn down the job.

596
00:42:21,160 --> 00:42:24,600
What does the contract say about resigning

597
00:42:25,600 --> 00:42:28,760
without giving 120 days' notice?

598
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:35,520
That's right.

599
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:40,680
You have to pay a penalty
of five times your salary.

600
00:42:45,560 --> 00:42:47,080
Can you afford that?

601
00:42:50,880 --> 00:42:53,320
Can someone like you afford it?

602
00:42:55,640 --> 00:42:56,680
Uh…

603
00:43:04,320 --> 00:43:05,520
Fine.

604
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:07,000
I'll do it.

605
00:43:08,080 --> 00:43:09,880
Good. So much for making a fuss.

606
00:43:10,360 --> 00:43:12,800
But I'm submitting my resignation notice today.

607
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:15,600
I'll work the full 120 days.

608
00:43:20,080 --> 00:43:21,440
Fine by me.

609
00:43:28,400 --> 00:43:29,760
Impressive.

610
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:31,560
Very impressive.

611
00:43:43,680 --> 00:43:44,880
From now on,

612
00:43:45,520 --> 00:43:46,920
prepare to fall apart,

613
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:48,760
Uttawadee.

614
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:51,520
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

615
00:43:51,600 --> 00:43:54,960
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

616
00:43:55,040 --> 00:44:00,080
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

617
00:44:00,160 --> 00:44:03,480
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

618
00:44:03,560 --> 00:44:07,800
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

619
00:44:07,880 --> 00:44:14,880
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

620
00:44:16,080 --> 00:44:22,640
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪

621
00:44:25,600 --> 00:44:28,400
Did you really think I'd trust you
to take care of my mother?

622
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:30,040
If you don't trust me,

623
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:31,360
why are you keeping me here?

624
00:44:31,920 --> 00:44:33,080
Don't put it that way.

625
00:44:33,160 --> 00:44:35,640
Someone like you
isn't worth keeping around.

626
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:38,960
Your smile disappears
the moment you see me.

627
00:44:39,040 --> 00:44:41,440
You must have wanted
to be a doctor's wife so badly.

628
00:44:50,560 --> 00:44:53,000
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

629
00:44:53,080 --> 00:44:56,680
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

630
00:44:56,760 --> 00:45:01,880
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

631
00:45:01,960 --> 00:45:05,080
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

632
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:09,600
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

633
00:45:09,680 --> 00:45:16,680
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

634
00:45:17,800 --> 00:45:24,160
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪
